course: dictionary
lesson: 5199
title: Jain, the name of a faith
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A Jain is a person who follows Jainism, an old religion from India. As an adjective, Jain describes things that belong to that faith, such as a Jain temple. «Diwali is the festival of lights, celebrated by Hindus, Sikhs and Jains with lamps, sweets and fireworks.» Here Jains means the people who follow the faith.
explain: Jainism teaches ahimsa, which means doing no harm. «A snail is a living creature; killing animals for fun is unkind, and Buddhists and Jains try not to harm any living thing at all.» So Jains try hard not to harm any living thing, even tiny creatures.
explain: Jain is the name of a faith, so it always starts with a capital letter, just like Hindu and Sikh. When you see a capital J, ask: is this a religion, or the people who follow it? If so, it is Jain.
fact: A Jain is a follower of Jainism, an old religion from India.
fact: Jainism teaches ahimsa, which means doing no harm to any living thing.
fact: Many Jains are strictly vegetarian, and some monks sweep the path so they do not step on insects.
fact: Jain is written with a capital letter because it is the name of a faith.
fact: Jain is also a family name in India.
exercise: «Diwali is the festival of lights, celebrated by Hindus, Sikhs and Jains with lamps, sweets and fireworks.» Who celebrates Diwali along with Hindus and Sikhs? | Mughal emperors | Snails | *Jains | Stone-age hunters
exercise: What does Jain mean in «a Jain temple»? | A tall building in the mountains | A kind of sweet | *Belonging to Jainism | A large lamp used at night
exercise: «Buddhists and Jains try not to harm any living thing at all.» Why do Jains try not to harm living things? | They are on a school trip | They enjoy scaring animals | Snails are dangerous | *Their faith teaches ahimsa, which means doing no harm
test: Which word means a follower of Jainism? | Jam | Janitor | *Jain | Jaguar
test: Why do some Jain monks sweep the path? | To find lost coins | To make the path wet | *So they do not step on insects | To keep the path warm
exam: Which sentence is written correctly? | jains try not to harm any Living thing | jains try not to harm any living thing | *Jains try not to harm any living thing | Jains try not to Harm any living thing
